A||||7||Shaft||85 GT vs. 87GT||||5||
Z||000000||Shaft||11-19-2000||01:40 AM||||How does an 85 GT compare to a newer Fiero like an 87? I know the 88's have a lot of different stuff so I'm mainly interested in the 85 vs other pre-88's.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||11-19-2000||02:02 AM||||The biggest difference is the transmission. '87 V6's were available with 5 spds, while 85 V6's were available with 4 spds. Both years used the same 3 spd auto.<BR>Antoher difference is in the headlight motors. 86 and older used loud, clunky units prone to failure. '87 and later used quiet, smotthly operating units that last longer.<BR>The body style is different. The fastback was available in '87, but not in '85, and not for most of '86<BR>Power mirrors were introduced for '85 or '86.<BR>15x7 mesh wheels were introduced in '85 or '86 (correct me if I'm wrong here).<BR>Factory subwoofer becamse availabel aobut that same time frame.<BR>'84's had speakers in the headrests, which were not used for any other year.<BR>Blue was only available n '87<BR>Any other details can be posted by someone more nit-picky than I.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||11-19-2000||08:17 AM||||Ok, If I'm nit picky than I'm sorry.lol<P>The 85GT also has the speakers in the headrests.In 86-88 there are 4x6 plate speakers in the pilars behind the seats.Factory subwoofer was for 86-88 GTs.<BR>The Lace type wheels became available in 86 for the GTs.<P>I that's about all I can think of.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-19-2000||08:59 AM||||The HVAC servo motors are silent in my '87 GT, but they are really noisey in my friends '86 (really noisey!!). Not sure if they made a change or if his are just worn out. I've had several Fieros, but I never noticed a difference till he pointed it out to me.<P>Also the '87-'88s have the engraved plenum instead of a decal. They also have an improved air intake tube. They also have improved exhaust manifolds withbetter welds and larger flanges and slotted holes so they can 'float' without cracking, but they still crack anyway. Pre-87 cars were supposed to be uprgraded with the newer manifolds, but many weren't.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||11-19-2000||09:53 AM||||Will,<P>Just for your info:<BR>Power mirrors were avaiable for ALL model years.<BR>The GT Fastback body style was avaiable for the entire '86 model year. (No notchback GT's  in '86, PERIOD!)<BR>The 15 inch wheels were standard equipment from '86 on for GT's.<BR>Factory sub: I''m not absoultly sure on that one, but I think that it was an option for all of '86 on up.<BR>2xsess is correct on the speakers as well.<BR>The 5-speed transmission (Getrag) was introduced mid-year '86 for V-6 cars..||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-19-2000||10:14 AM||||From a bodystyle standpoint, I'd take the '85 every time.<P>Indyresto posted everything I planned to.||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||11-19-2000||01:10 PM||||I'm with Fiero56. Is'nt the 85' GT faster? <BR>I think the 85' was the lightest GT, therfore the fastest...not really noticable.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||11-19-2000||02:49 PM||||87's have a bigger gas tank too.||||reg||1
